# FinnOS application registry
#
# The catalogue of apps the OS knows about. It ships with the OS and says what
# each app is called, what it looks like and what runs it — never whether it
# is on this machine. That belongs to the package manager, which keeps its
# own list in /var/lib/finnpkg/installed.
#
# Format: id | Name | icon | command | note
#
#   id       the name the rest of the system uses
#   Name     what the user sees
#   icon     an SVG in /usr/share/finn/icons
#   command  what to run when the app is launched
#   note     free text, shown as the app's detail line
#
# The first-party apps are the ones NAMING.md reserves the family name for.
# The names are the brand and a plain English noun: Finn Code, Finn Files.

code    | Finn Code     | code.svg     | /usr/bin/finn-code    | Editor
files   | Finn Files    | files.svg    | /usr/bin/finn-files   | File manager
notes   | Finn Notes    | notes.svg    | /usr/bin/finn-notes   | Notes
studio  | Finn Studio   | studio.svg   | /usr/bin/finn-studio  | Visual FinnUI designer
store   | Finn Store    | store.svg    | /usr/bin/finn-store   | App distribution
sync    | Finn Sync     | sync.svg     | /usr/bin/finn-sync    | Device-to-device sync
vault   | Finn Vault    | vault.svg    | /usr/bin/finn-vault   | Credentials and keys
term    | Finn Terminal | terminal.svg | /usr/bin/finn-term    | Shell host
